    { math: '3 · The cognitive effects debate', note: 'Does bilingualism sharpen executive function (the "bilingual advantage")? Early studies said yes; large replications are mixed. Honest current position: small or no general advantage, but the experience of managing two systems is real and lifelong.' },
    { math: '4 · Language and thought: the Sapir–Whorf question', note: 'The strong version (language determines thought) is false; the weak version has support — Russian speakers discriminate blues faster (separate words for light/dark blue), spatial metaphors shape reasoning. Language nudges thought; it doesn\'t imprison it.' },
